  "closes": [
    "Closes the 'MRbar/d2 x EWMA/CUSUM cross' open item shared by estparam-memory-detector-arl-degradation-v1 and moving-range-arl-degradation-v1.",
    "Recomputes the module's guaranteed 30-batch union false-alarm table under the sigma estimator the Individuals chart actually defaults to.",
    "Directly tests whether the previously-reported smallest_tabulated_m_meeting_criterion=50 survives the switch from S/c4 (upper bound, per prior receipt's own caveat) to MRbar/d2 (operating estimator)."
  ],
  "detector_design": {
    "cusum_h": 5.0,
    "cusum_k": 0.5,
    "ewma_L": 3.0,
    "ewma_lambda": 0.2,
    "note": "All three charts read the SAME standardized stream off the SAME Phase-I baseline in the live module; if the Individuals chart uses MRbar/d2 the EWMA/CUSUM arms operate on that same estimate.",
    "shewhart_individuals_L": 3.0,
    "sigma_estimator": "MRbar/d2(2), d2(2)=2/sqrt(pi) (Montgomery default for Individuals charts; NIST/SEMATECH 6.3.2)"
  },
  "does_not_close": [
    "Does NOT establish real-batch acceptability, product qualification, EHS acceptability, or batch-release authority.",
    "Assumes i.i.d. normal in-control data; autocorrelation and non-normality are not modeled and remain open.",
    "The union false-alarm figure is a per-node sum of 30/ARL0 across the three arms sharing one (U,W) draw; it is still a Bonferroni-style rate approximation of the union alarm event, not an exact union probability.",
    "The Lucas-Crosier two-sided CUSUM 1/ARL=1/ARL+ +1/ARL- combination is an approximation (validated to <=6% against Montgomery Table 9.4 in the prior receipt).",
    "The W sampling law is characterized by Monte Carlo (no closed form for MRbar/d2), so the reported percentiles carry MC sampling noise on top of the exact conditional-ARL formula; quantified by the grid-convergence gate.",
    "No prospective time-ordered 30-batch pilot is checked in; this is a theory characterization, not a false-alarm measurement on real batches.",
    "Out-of-control (ARL1) performance under MRbar/d2-estimated parameters, and the recall >=90% half of the KPI, are not characterized here.",
    "Covers only the span-2 moving range d2(2); larger MR spans are not characterized."
  ],
